Let the MSP430 C library call the reentrant system calls

By default, newlib expects the system calls of MSP430 to be provided without
a leading underscore, and does not build the POSIX system call wrappers
(read(), write() and so on). RIOT provides the reentrant system calls
(_read_r(), _write_r() and so on) instead, like it does for other
architectures. Therefore, the wrappers are built to call the reentrant
system calls directly, which newlib does not provide itself.

--- a/newlib/configure.host
+++ b/newlib/configure.host
@@ -791,6 +791,10 @@
 	default_newlib_io_long_long="yes"
 	newlib_cflags="${newlib_cflags} -Os -DPREFER_SIZE_OVER_SPEED -DSMALL_MEMORY"
         ;;
+  msp430*-*-*)
+	newlib_cflags="${newlib_cflags} -DREENTRANT_SYSCALLS_PROVIDED"
+	syscall_dir=syscalls
+	;;
   nios2*)
 	syscall_dir=
 	newlib_cflags="${newlib_cflags} -DHAVE_RENAME -DHAVE_SYSTEM -DMISSING_SYSCALL_NAMES"
